.TH LINK 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
link \- create a hard link
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.B int link(const char* oldpath, const char* newpath);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates newpath as a hard link to oldpath.  Linux does not dereference a
symbolic link in oldpath.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero, or \-1 with errno set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR symlink (3crunch),
.BR unlink (3crunch),
.BR link (2)
